{"id":9623,"date":"2025-10-27T06:49:20","date_gmt":"2025-10-27T06:49:20","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/?p=9623"},"modified":"2026-08-07T07:21:40","modified_gmt":"2026-08-07T07:21:40","slug":"do-follow-vs-no-follow-backlinks","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/do-follow-vs-no-follow-backlinks\/","title":{"rendered":"Do follow vs. No follow Backlinks (Difference &amp; Comparison)"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p>Those new to <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-is-seo\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">SEO<\/a> might wonder what all the commotion is about do follow links vs. no follow links. Confused? Don&#8217;t worry; we are going to clear it all up.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>One of the first things you need to learn about link-building is to differentiate between do follow and no follow links. While these two might seem like two identical elements, they can\u2019t be more different in terms of the value they provide. Specifically, a high-quality do follow link can completely change the outlook of your site, which can\u2019t be said for no follow links.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>This blog will examine the difference between do follow and no follow backlinks, how they impact your overall SEO efforts, and much more. Keep reading to learn more!<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>What is do follow Link?<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>do follow links let Google and other search engines point back to your website or blog. So, every time you insert a do follow link on your website, it can point back to you, strengthening your authority by showing search engines what other websites, posts, and blogs are linking to you.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Here\u2019s what a do follow link appears to be:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<pre class=\"wp-block-code\"><code>&lt;a href=\u201dexample.com\u201d&gt;anchor text here&lt;\/a&gt;<\/code><\/pre>\n\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/search-engines\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Search engines<\/a> follow every website link unless you add a rel=\u201dno follow\u201d tag. For instance, if you link to another site in your content, that link is a do follow link by default. A search engine considers your link a vote of confidence for the website you are linking to.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Further, if a website links to your site by default, it signals to search engines that your website is a valuable resource. So, strive to build do follow backlinks. To know more about backlinks, read our blog on <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-are-backlinks\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">What are Backlinks in SEO?<\/a>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n    <!-- LOTTIE SCRIPT -->\n    <script src=\"https:\/\/unpkg.com\/@lottiefiles\/lottie-player@latest\/dist\/lottie-player.js\"><\/script>\n\n    <section class=\"wscube-courses mb-2\">\n        <div class=\"container\">\n            <h3 class=\"mb-4\">Recommended Professional <\/br> Certificates<\/h3>\n\n            <div class=\"owl-carousel courseOwl\">\n\n                \n                    \n                    <div class=\"course-card card-r rounded-4\">\n\n                        <!-- \u2705 SINGLE MEDIA DIV (FIXED) -->\n                        <div class=\"course-media\"\n                             data-lottie=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/uploads\/images\/courses\/json-images\/digital-marketing.json\"\n                             data-fallback=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/themes\/newwscube\/assets\/imges\/Image.png\">\n                        <\/div>\n\n                        <div class=\"card-body\">\n                            <h5>AI-Powered Digital Marketing Course<\/h5>\n\n                            <p class=\"rating\">\n                                4.9 \u2605\u2605\u2605\u2605\u2605\n                                (19476)\n                            <\/p>\n\n                            <ul class=\"course-meta\">