uilding Mistakes<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/on-page-seo-factors\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">On Page SEO Factors<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/ai-seo-tools\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">AI SEO Tools<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/on-page-seo-checklist\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">On Page SEO Checklist<\/a><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Common Scenarios to Use no follow Links<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>1. Sponsored or Paid Links<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p>If you receive compensation for including a link on your site, mark it as no follow. This adheres to Google\u2019s guidelines and prevents potential penalties for manipulative link schemes.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>2. User-Generated Content<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p>Use no follow and ugc attributes for links in comments, forums, and other user-generated areas. This helps deter spammers from gaming the system to boost rankings.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>3. Untrusted or Low-Quality Sources<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p>If linking to an untrustworthy or low-quality website, use no follow to signal you don\u2019t necessarily endorse or vouch for that site.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>4. Login\/Registration Pages<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p>It\u2019s best practice to no follow links to login, registration, or account areas, as these typically lack valuable content for search crawlers.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>5. Affiliate or Partnership Links<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p>For affiliate or partner links where you earn referral commissions, use no follow and sponsored attributes to comply with search engine guidelines regarding paid links.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Also Read:<\/strong> <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/meta-title-description-length\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Meta Title and Meta Description Length Guidelines<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Benefits of no follow Links<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Here are the benefits of no follow links for SEO:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Increased Brand Awareness and Exposure:<\/strong> While no follow links don\u2019t directly impact rankings, they can increase brand visibility and drive referral traffic.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Potential do follow Link Acquisition:<\/strong> Participating in communities and platforms that allow no follow links can establish relationships leading to future do follow opportunities.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Compliance with Guidelines:<\/strong> Using no follow for sponsored content, user-generated comments, and untrusted sources demonstrates adherence to search engine guidelines, avoiding potential penalties.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Crawl Budget Optimization:<\/strong> Using no follow for low-value or irrelevant pages helps search engines prioritize crawling your most important content.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Advertising Disclosures:<\/strong> no follow links disclose sponsored or paid links, promoting transparency and trust.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-white-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-background-color has-text-color has-background has-link-color wp-elements-d72f351059e80039135382f58233f821\"><strong>Explore Our Most Popular Marketing Courses<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/digital-marketing-course?utm_source=WsBlog&amp;utm_medium=BlogTable&amp;utm_campaign=seo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Digital Marketing Course<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/performance-marketing-course?utm_source=WsBlog&amp;utm_medium=BlogTable&amp;utm_campaign=seo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Performance Marketing Course<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/seo-course?utm_source=WsBlog&amp;utm_medium=BlogInterlink&amp;utm_campaign=seo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">SEO Course<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/ai-course?utm_source=WsBlog&amp;utm_medium=BlogInterlink&amp;utm_campaign=seo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">AI Course<\/a><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>3 Major Differences Between do follow and no follow Links<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Here\u2019s how these two <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/backlinks-types\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">types of backlinks<\/a> differ between each other:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>1. SEO Value<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>no follow and do follow links differ in terms of their SEO value. While do follows benefit your website, only a few no follows are useful for your brand. A do follow link will pass link juice from another website to yours, thus improving its authority and reputation in search engines.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>However, that doesn\u2019t mean a no follow backlink is entirely useless. You still get direct traffic from other websites, which can sometimes be immense when featured on a large platform. That way, you can grow awareness and potentially score additional indirect links.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>2. Indexing<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>One of the major functions of SERPs, Google crawlers crawl all over your website, looking for valuable content. They rely heavily on sitemaps and your architecture to get from one page to another. Among others, they also use links to reach specific content.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Google bots use do follow backlinks to discover new pages on your website. These links help with link equity on the internet, significantly improving visibility and hastening the indexability of platforms that accrue many links. On the other hand, a no follow link doesn\u2019t provide that value, as bots will not follow it. <\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>3. Spam Prevention<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>The no follow attribute is crucial for preventing comment spam and other SEO tactics for gaining links. These hyperlinks are commonly used for forum posts and social media sharing that would allow marketers to accrue lots of high-quality do follow links with minimal effort.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>As these platforms automatically put a no follow tag on each link on their site, there\u2019s no way to manipulate these platforms to boost your website. In other words, you won\u2019t gain significant marketing benefits from user-generated content besides direct traffic and brand awareness.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Do follow vs. No follow Links: Which is the Best for External Links?<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>You are probably wondering which you should use for your external links. Don\u2019t worry. We have you covered.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Use no follow Link:<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>You don\u2019t want to endorse a website<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place a sponsored link on your website<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add affiliate links to your website<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Visitors are allowed to insert links on your website via UGC<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>You want to protect yourself from Google&#8217;s penalties<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Use do follow Link:<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Now that you know when to use no follow links for external links, you\u2019re probably wondering when to use the do follow attribute to a link. Use the do follow attribute when:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Linking to an authoritative website<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Endorsing a valuable resource for your users<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p>Use the do follow tag signals to search engines that you endorse the website you are pointing to; for example, if the site is dubious, search engines will connect you with that dodgy website. So be cautious when linking out to other websites in your content. Use only the do follow attribute when you are sure the website is reputable. Aiming to build a reputable website and drive more organic traffic, join an <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/seo-course?utm_source=WsBlog&amp;utm_medium=BlogInterlink&amp;utm_campaign=traffic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">SEO course<\/a> taught by industry experts.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Also Read:<\/strong> <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-seo-expert\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">How to Become an SEO Expert?<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Do Follow vs No Follow Backlinks (Video)<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<iframe loading=\"lazy\" width=\"640\" height=\"350\" src=\"https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/embed\/kO9IJaIrSLE?si=Vk76c6pLIugETvzU\" title=\"YouTube video player\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen><\/iframe>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>FAQs on do follow vs. no follow Links<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"schema-faq wp-block-yoast-faq-block\"><div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1716803266329\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">1. <strong>What is the difference between do follow and no follow links?<\/strong><\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Backlinks fall into two major categories: do follow and no follow. do follow links pass link juice and help your website\u2019s SEO. Conversely, no follow links do not pass any link juice and don\u2019t affect your website\u2019s SEO. Usually, no follow backlinks are used for links the website owner does not want to endorse.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1716803281843\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">2. <strong>What is the ratio of do follow and no follow links?<\/strong><\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">A good thumb rule is to aim for 60% do follow and 40% no follow links. Remember that both links are necessary for the long-term success of your website. This is because many high-authority websites offer only nofollow links, which still brings tremendous benefits regarding SEO and web traffic.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1716803309756\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">3. <strong>Why use no follow links?<\/strong><\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">no follow links can link to poor-quality websites or those that search engines consider spammy. If you are writing a blog and wish to cite your source, but the source is on a low-quality website, you might use no follow links to prevent your website from passing authority to another.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1716803330705\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">4. <strong>Is do follow good for backlinks?<\/strong><\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">A strong backlink profile must have a mix of do follow and no follow links. It&#8217;s best to acquire high-quality, relevant do follow links. But no follow links can also drive traffic and increase brand awareness.\u00a0<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1716803354610\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">5. <strong>What are the benefits of having a mix of no follow and do follow backlinks?<\/strong><\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Several benefits come with having a mix of no follow and do follow backlinks:<br\/>&#8211; Increase your rankings and visibility<br\/>&#8211; Create a natural link profile, improving your website\u2019s credibility<br\/>&#8211; A mix of do follow and no follow links creates a multiple-link folio, mitigating several risks.<\/p> <\/div> <\/div>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/seo-course?utm_source=WsBlog&amp;utm_medium=Content_Banner&amp;utm_campaign=SEO&amp;utm_page=\/do-follow-vs-no-follow-backlinks\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1000\" height=\"250\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/seo-training.webp\" alt=\"seo training\" class=\"wp-image-6524\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/seo-training.webp 1000w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/seo-training-300x75.webp 300w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/seo-training-768x192.webp 768w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/02\/seo-training-150x38.webp 150w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px\" \/><\/a><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Conclusion<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>In conclusion, backlinks are a key element of SEO and should be integrated into your online marketing strategy. While do follow backlinks help improve your website&#8217;s authority and relevance, no follow backlinks can be useful for traffic and diversifying your link profile. However, it&#8217;s important to focus on quality rather than quantity of links and work with relevant and reliable websites to maximize the benefits.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-white-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-background-color has-text-color has-backgrou